{"name":"Guide Pink","hex":"#eb4962","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guide","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who guides, especially someone hired to show people around a place or an institution and offer information and explanation, or to lead them through dangerous terrain.","A document or book that offers information or instruction; guidebook."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To serve as a guide for someone or something; to lead or direct in a way; to conduct in a course or path.","To steer or navigate, especially a ship or as a pilot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guide"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guide","blocks":[{"text":"A guide is a person who leads travelers, sportspeople, or tourists through unknown or unfamiliar locations. The term can also be applied to a person who leads others to more abstract goals such as knowledge or wisdom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Anselm_Klotz%28L%29-Josef_Frey%28R%29.jpg/330px-Anselm_Klotz%28L%29-Josef_Frey%28R%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guide","wikidata":"Q14290559"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tourguide2.jpg/500px-Tourguide2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tourguide2.jpg/1280px-Tourguide2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tourguide2.jpg/500px-Tourguide2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tour guide at the Centre Block in Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATourguide2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Raquette_River_-_at_Sweeney_Carry.jpg/500px-Raquette_River_-_at_Sweeney_Carry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Raquette_River_-_at_Sweeney_Carry.jpg/500px-Raquette_River_-_at_Sweeney_Carry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adirondack guides (carrying and rowing guideboats on the Raquette River, 1888","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaquette_River_-_at_Sweeney_Carry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Jim_Bridger.jpg/500px-Jim_Bridger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Jim_Bridger.jpg/500px-Jim_Bridger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Famed mountain man Jim Bridger served as guide and army scout during the first Powder River Expedition in 1865 against the Sioux and Cheyenne in Dakota and Montana Territories.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJim_Bridger.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki